{"species": "items_list", "value": [["Miracle Seed", "73.5", "Holder's Grass-type attacks have 1.2× power.", [18, 4]], ["Life Orb", "17.7", "Holder's attacks do 1.3× damage, and it loses 1/10 its max HP after the attack.", [15, 9]], ["Eject Button", "3.2", "If holder survives a hit, it immediately switches out to a chosen ally. Single use.", [7, 6]], ["Occa Berry", "2.6", "Halves damage taken from a supereffective Fire-type attack. Single use.", [19, 7]], ["Sitrus Berry", "1.3", "Restores 1/4 max HP when at 1/2 max HP or less. Single use.", [28, 0]], ["Grassy Seed", "0.6", "If the terrain is Grassy Terrain, raises holder's Defense by 1 stage. Single use.", [41, 11]], ["Kebia Berry", "0.3", "Halves damage taken from a supereffective Poison-type attack. Single use.", [14, 10]], ["Leftovers", "0.3", "At the end of every turn, holder restores 1/16 of its max HP.", [15, 2]], ["Iron Ball", "0.3", "Holder is grounded, Speed halved. If Flying type, takes neutral Ground damage.", [14, 0]]], "tournament_id": "2027_gdansk_pok_mon_vgc_regional_championships"}
{"species": "moves_list", "value": [["Fake Out", "100.0", "Normal (Physical)\nBase Power: 40\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 3\nHas a 100% chance to make the target flinch. Fails unless it is the user's first turn on the field."], ["Grassy Glide", "99.7", "Grass (Physical)\nBase Power: 55\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nIf the current terrain is Grassy Terrain and the user is grounded, this move has its priority increased by 1."], ["Wood Hammer", "93.9", "Grass (Physical)\nBase Power: 120\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nIf the target lost HP, the user takes recoil damage equal to 33% the HP lost by the target, rounded half up, but not less than 1 HP."], ["High Horsepower", "50.6", "Ground (Physical)\nBase Power: 95\nAccuracy: 95\nPriority: 0\nNo additional effect."], ["U-turn", "43.9", "Bug (Physical)\nBase Power: 70\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nIf this move is successful and the user has not fainted, the user switches out even if it is trapped and is replaced immediately by a selected party member. The user does not switch out if there are no unfainted party members, or if the target switched out using an Eject Button or through the effect of the Emergency Exit or Wimp Out Abilities."], ["Protect", "7.4", "Normal (Status)\nBase Power: N/A\nAccuracy: N/A\nPriority: 4\nThe user is protected from most attacks made by other Pokemon during this turn. This move has a 1/X chance of being successful, where X starts at 1 and triples each time this move is successfully used. X resets to 1 if this move fails, if the user's last move used is not Baneful Bunker, Burning Bulwark, Detect, Endure, King's Shield, Max Guard, Obstruct, Protect, Quick Guard, Silk Trap, Spiky Shield, or Wide Guard, or if it was one of those moves and the user's protection was broken. Fails if the user moves last this turn."], ["Superpower", "2.3", "Fighting (Physical)\nBase Power: 120\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nLowers the user's Attack and Defense by 1 stage."], ["Drum Beating", "1.3", "Grass (Physical)\nBase Power: 80\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nHas a 100% chance to lower the target's Speed by 1 stage."], ["Taunt", "0.3", "Dark (Status)\nBase Power: N/A\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nPrevents the target from using non-damaging moves for its next three turns. Pokemon with the Oblivious Ability or protected by the Aroma Veil Ability are immune."], ["Drain Punch", "0.3", "Fighting (Physical)\nBase Power: 75\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nThe user recovers 1/2 the HP lost by the target, rounded half up. If Big Root is held by the user, the HP recovered is 1.3× normal, rounded half down."], ["Knock Off", "0.3", "Dark (Physical)\nBase Power: 65\nAccuracy: 100\nPriority: 0\nThis move's power is multiplied by 1.5 if the target is holding an item, and the target loses its held item if the user has not fainted. A target with the Sticky Hold Ability does not lose its held item if it has not fainted. This move does not increase in power or remove the target's item if it is a Blue Orb, Red Orb, Adamant Crystal, Lustrous Globe, Griseous Core, Plate, Drive, Memory, Rusted Sword, Rusted Shield, Booster Energy, or Mask held by a Kyogre, Groudon, Dialga, Palkia, Giratina, Arceus, Genesect, Silvally, Zacian, Zamazenta, Paradox Pokemon, or Ogerpon, respectively, or if the user is one of those species and the target is holding the respective item. In this case, Paradox Pokemon include every species with the Protosynthesis and Quark Drive Abilities, except Gouging Fire, Raging Bolt, Iron Boulder, and Iron Crown. Items lost to this move cannot be regained with Recycle or the Harvest Ability."]], "tournament_id": "2027_gdansk_pok_mon_vgc_regional_championships"}
